  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user picking a smiley or a GIF, and above all with VoiceOver or Switch Control, I want the detail to open inside the picker with a visible way back, so that I am never three modal layers deep with a swipe as the only exit.\n\n### Rule\n\n- \"Display only one sheet at a time from the main interface. […] If something people do within a sheet results in another sheet appearing, close the first sheet before displaying the new one.\" — [HIG › Sheets](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sheets) (Best practices; page updated 2026-03-24).\n- \"Offer alternatives to gestures. […] For example, if you use a swipe gesture to dismiss a view, also make a button available so people can tap or use an assistive device.\" — [HIG › Accessibility](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/accessibility) (Mobility; updated 2025-06-09).\n- \"Make it easy to identify a modal view's task.\" — [HIG › Modality](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/modality).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- The composer is already a sheet or a full-screen cover (`App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ReaderComposerPresenter.swift:45-47`); it presents the smiley picker as a sheet (`Composer/ReplyComposerView.swift:117-119`).\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Smileys/SmileyPickerView.swift:66-69`: the picker presents `.sheet(item: $model.presented) { SmileyDetailView(…).presentationDetents([.medium, .large]) }`. `SmileyDetailView` (`:283-300`) is a bare `VStack` (image, code, « Insérer », favourite button, keywords): no `NavigationStack`, toolbar, title or close button. The only ways out are a swipe down or « Insérer ».\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/Gif/GifPickerView.swift:36-43`: `.sheet(item: $model.selected) { GifConfirmationView… }` over the GIF sheet: the same third layer.\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nTwo layers only: the panels are sheets over the composer (`HFRswift/Swift/AnswerView.swift:499-523`); the smiley detail is an in-panel card (`:2140`, `:2605`) with an `xmark` button labelled « Fermer » (`:2496-2509`). SwiftHFR's header records \"detail is a sheet instead of an overlay card\" as a lot decision.\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect**: the missing close button is an accessibility matter and worse than legacy.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- Push the smiley detail and the GIF confirmation inside the panel's existing `NavigationStack` (`navigationDestination(item:)`): the system back button and an inline title come with it, and the third layer goes.\n- Check: at most two presentation layers when a detail is open; VoiceOver reaches a back or close element. Mac check on iPhone and iPad. Coordinate with #909 (the picker closing on the first tap), which touches the same flow.\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
